Production employee
Day Shift / 21-40 hours per week / Utrecht
🌟 In short

  - Fixed day shift hours (07:00-16:30)

  - Choose your workweek: 3, 4, or 5 fixed weekdays

  - Clean working environment

💼 The position

As a production employee, you ensure that hotels and restaurants are supplied daily with fresh, clean linen. This includes items such as napkins, tablecloths, towels, pillowcases, and duvet covers. Using modern machines, the linen is washed, ironed, and folded. You will be actively working and moving throughout the day 💪.

Together with your colleagues, you make sure everything runs smoothly. Your main tasks include:

  - Sorting the linen;

  - Loading the linen into the machines piece by piece;

  - Checking the quality;

  - Placing stacks of linen neatly into the roll containers.

💰 What we offer

  - Starting salary of € 15.33 gross per hour (€ 14.99 + € 0.34 allowance);

  - After 6 months: € 15.45 gross per hour + € 0.82 year-end allowance (5.33%);;

  - Flexible workweek: choose 3, 4, or 5 fixed weekdays;

  - A Stable job with fixed working hours;

  - 25 vacation days, 8.33% holiday pay, and travel allowance (5–40 km one way);

  - Career growth opportunities, e.g., to shift supervisor or operator.

👀 What we expect from you

  - You speak Dutch or English;

  - You live in the Utrecht area (within 25 km of our laundry);

  - You are available for at least 3 fixed weekdays (07:00 – 16:30);

  - You are proactive and enjoy staying active;

  - You have a flexible work attitude.

📞 Interested?

For more information or to apply, contact Hester Visser (HR):

📞 Call: 030 307 2200

 💬 WhatsApp: 06 2539 7485

 📧 Email: werkenbij@vanderkleijtextiel.nl

Or view the vacancy online on our website:

https://werkenbij.vanderkleijtextiel.nl/en/production-personnel/

    Interesse in de functie van Production employee bij Wasserij & Linnenverhuur G. van der Kleij & Zn. bv regio Utrecht?

Reageer nu met je CV en motivatie v

SamenvattingReady for the next step in production? Contribute to quality and efficiency! In this role, you are responsible for disassembling, cleaning, testing, and reassembling returned products. This way, you give electronics a second life and directly contribute to a more sustainable process. Do you enjoy varied work and work with precision? Then this is your opportunity!Over de functieYour responsibilities include:
- disassembling returned modems, routers, and parts;
- cleaning components and devices;
- testing individual components and complete products;
- assembling refurbished devices;
- accurately recording test outcomes.

In this company you work from monday to friday, from 07:30 till 16:30.
Over het bedrijfThis company offers comprehensive logistics services with a strong focus on sustainability. They turn returned electronics into valuable refurbished products using high quality and efficient processes.
Wat wij vragen- Energetic and able to stand for 8 hours;
- Interest in electronics and technical tasks;
- Reasonable English language skills;
- Precise, motivated, and team-oriented.

Wat wij bieden- Hourly wage starting from €15.26
- Holiday allowance and vacation hours accrual
- Travel allowance / reimbursement
- High chance of a permanent contract after 6 months
- Realistic opportunities for personal and professional development
- Monthly drinks / social gatherings
- Working in a close-knit and friendly team

Meer informatieWill you start working as a production worker in Bleiswijk? You can apply within just 2 minutes.
Any questions? Thomas will be happy to help you via +31 6 237 235 54 (also WhatsApp) or by email at t.dupuis@carriere.com.
